Are liches fleshy in the first place?  Most depictions I've seen in
non-nethack sources have them as something more like a skeleton.
(See, for instance, the lich portraits in Battle for Wesnoth, or Xykon
in the Order of the Stick comic.)  Not a lot of flesh there.

The nethack wiki article on Liches says they never leave corpses,
and the article on stone to flesh seems to indicate that monsters
that don't leave corpses may be treated differently in some edge
cases, although nothing specifically says their statues can't be
eanimated in the usual case.  (It does say statues can't be
reanimated if their race has been genocided, but I'm guessing
you probably knew that much.)

This whole question sounds like a good candidate for
wizard-mode testing.


